# .git IS shipped. Installing git without it would be worse than neither:
# the binary exists, `git ls-files` exits 128 in a directory that is not a
# repository, and a scan built on it returns an EMPTY set -- so every
# structural guard passes having examined nothing.
.venv
.snakemake
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
verification/
# Nothing tracked is excluded: container_verify.sh runs the manifest check
# in the image, and a governed file missing from it would fail that check
# (hosted run 32618887858). tests/test_container_manifest_coverage.py fails
# if a pattern here starts hiding a governed file.
__pycache__
*.pyc
